Finding: {"title":"Equipment profile edit applies optimistic local state update with no rollback on save failure","severity":"MEDIUM","area":"Data Integrity / Frontend State","files":["src/components/features/mvp-v2/pages/equipment-profile.tsx"],"detail":"`handleSaveEdit` (lines 1004-1076) calls `setEq(updated)` at line 1068 BEFORE `await persistEquipmentUpdate(updated)` at line 1069. If the PUT request fails, the catch block (lines 1072-1074) only shows an error toast — it never reverts `eq` back to the pre-edit server state.","impact":"After a failed save, the UI continues to display the user's unsaved edits (weight & balance figures, TBO hours, status, etc.) as if they succeeded, even though the server still holds the old values. A page refresh or navigation away/back silently reverts to the real (older) data, which will read as data loss/corruption to the user who believed the save succeeded from the UI's own display.","recommendation":"Capture the pre-edit `eq` value, and in the catch block call `setEq(previousEq)` to roll back the optimistic update on failure — or defer `setEq(updated)` until after `persistEquipmentUpdate` resolves successfully.","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

